# Homework 1 Reproducible Run Instructions

Run these commands from the repository root.

## Part 1 checks

```bash
node code/web_application/tests/run-tests.js
```

## Build and run the web application with Docker

```bash
docker build -f code/Dockerfile -t hw1-rental-listings:1.0 .
docker run --detach --name s7838-rental-housing --publish 8638:80 hw1-rental-listings:1.0
```

Open http://localhost:8638 in a browser.

Stop the local container when finished:

```bash
docker stop s7838-rental-housing
```

## Part 2: Agentic AI pipeline

Requires Ollama running locally with the qwen2:7b model pulled.

```bash
ollama serve
ollama pull qwen2:7b
```

In another terminal:

```bash
cd code
python3.11 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
python agents_demo.py
```

This prints the Planner output, Reviewer output, Finalizer step, and final published JSON (exactly 3 tags, summary of at most 25 words) to the console.

## Part 3: Non-determinism testing

Uses the same venv and Ollama setup as Part 2. The fixed test input is saved at
reports/hw01/cases/nondeterminism_input.json and must not be changed between runs.

```bash
cd code
source venv/bin/activate
python run_nondeterminism_tests.py
python analyze_nondeterminism.py
```

The first command runs agents_demo.py 40 times (20 at temperature 0.7, 20 at temperature 0.0)
against the fixed input and saves every result to reports/hw01/raw/nondeterminism_results.json.
The second command computes the distinct-tag-set and latency statistics and writes
reports/hw01/METRICS.md.

## Part 4: Model client and token accounting

Uses the same venv and Ollama setup as Part 2/3.

```bash
cd code
source venv/bin/activate
python hw1_client.py
```

This starts an interactive session. Type a message and press Enter to chat; type /stats
to print turn count, cumulative token counts, and the serialized conversation-history
length without calling the model; type /exit to quit and print the final cumulative
summary.
